# Every package releases.nomadware.io serves, in index order. One per line:
#
#   name | binary | description | source | post_install | kind | story
#
# name    the URL prefix (<base>/<name>/…); lowercase, digits, dashes
# binary  what install.sh installs; release assets are <binary>-<os>-<arch>
# source  optional: the package's public repo, https://github.com/fum4/<repo>; the index
#         links it beside the name. Leave it empty for a private package.
# post_install  optional: arguments for the installed binary, run once install.sh has
#         installed it (e.g. "setup" = run `<binary> setup`): offered as a [Y/n] prompt on a
#         terminal, printed as the next step otherwise. Arguments only, never shell: words of
#         lowercase letters, digits and dashes, separated by spaces (bin/render-install refuses
#         anything else). Not for a legacy package (it has no installer).
# kind    optional: "legacy" = no longer developed, no signed bucket, no installer. It is listed
#         in the index's Legacy section and downloads straight from the source repo's latest
#         GitHub release (needs a source; binary is unused there).
# story   optional, legacy only: https://nomadware.io/blog/<slug>, linked as "why it stopped".
# Adding a package: README.md § Adding a package.
